{
  "requirement": "The `Rust` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Rust;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Rust;\nimpl Debug for Rust;\nimpl Default for Rust;\nimpl OutlineLang for Rust;\nimpl Copy for Rust;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.rust.Rust` states that `Rust` is a public unit struct. It lists the trait implementations `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy`. It also says `Rust` supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules that the chapter describes. Those rules belong to the refining requirements `requirements.sdk.sources.rust.language`, `requirements.sdk.sources.rust.items` and `requirements.sdk.sources.rust.fingerprints`, so they need no separate test here.\n\nMapping of obligations to tests:\n- **Struct shape and trait implementations.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc for the SDK. It compares each declared item's declaration and its trait-implementation set (`check_declaration` and `trait_impls`) with the requirement text. A missing, extra or changed `Debug`, `Clone`, `Default`, `Copy` or `OutlineLang` implementation, or a changed struct form, would fail it.\n- **`Copy`, `Clone`, `Default` and `OutlineLang`, by behavior.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls its `check` helper with `languages::Rust`. The helper's bound `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` requires those traits at compile time. It asserts these results:\n  - the language's `extensions()` equal `[\"rs\"]`;\n  - `fingerprint_scheme()` is `rust-structural-v1`;\n  - the type has size 0;\n  - `Clone::clone` yields the same extensions;\n  - `Rust::default()` has the same fingerprint scheme.\n  \n  The same helper also checks outline output, selection, and structural search through the `OutlineLang` implementation.\n- **Rust item rules.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` checks Rust selectors, kinds, spans, doc and attribute attachment, and fingerprint stability under formatting and sensitivity to code changes.\n\nI found no obligation of the subject's own text that these tests leave unchecked.",
